Subject: [PATCH 131/148] docs(ci): describe the archive install, not the
 go-module flow (gcp-fooz4)

The release-compatibility design doc said the inference workflows
resolve gascity with `go mod download -json` and check out the module's
`.Origin.Hash`. It also said pack-release-compatibility runs
`go install ...@<ref>` and that the nightly runs against `gc@main`. All
of that predates patch 0075's archive install. The doc now says that gc
comes from the release archive, that the source commit is read from the
binary's vcs.revision with the tag as a fallback, and that `main` means
the rolling `edge` pre-release.

The gascity_ref input descriptions on both inference workflows still
gave go-module semantics, including commit SHAs and go's slash rule.
They now list the values that have an archive and say that a branch or
commit SHA fails the install.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
